<%# A block the CODE fills from the verified catalogue.

  THE OPERATOR OWNS THE COPY AND NOTHING ELSE. The heading, the standfirst and the link label come from the
  row; the entries, their availability state and their prerequisites come from Marketing::Catalog, which
  carries the evidence in docs/official-website/02-verified-feature-inventory.md. That split is the line this
  programme exists to hold: a conditional feature cannot be edited into an available one, because its state
  was never in the editor.

  THREE SHAPES, AND THE OPERATOR PICKS. `cards` is the index grid, `chips` is an inline strip, and `list` is
  the channel index. `list` exists because the home page carries TWO catalogue blocks in a row -- channels,
  then features -- and when both drew the same grid of bordered white cards the page became one
  undifferentiated field with no way to tell where a section began. Same entries, same honesty, different
  form.

  WHAT `list` NOW IS. It was nine full-width rows of hairline-separated text in a 13rem/auto split: the most
  important content on the site, set as a specification table, running half the height of the home page and
  leaving the outer third of a desktop window empty beside it. It is now a two-column index led by a glyph --
  no borders, no rules, the band's own field showing between the entries -- which halves the height, uses the
  measure, and still reads as something other than the card grid that follows it.
%>
<%# THE ENTRY HEADING LEVEL FOLLOWS THE SECTION'S OWN, exactly as sections/_cards.html.erb computes it. With a
  section heading the entries sit under an <h2> and are <h3>s; without one they are the first headings after
  the page's <h1> and must be <h2>s. Both shapes that print an entry name read this one value, because they
  disagreed: `list` was always an <h3> (so the home page's heading-less blocks skipped a level) and the card
  was always an <h2> (so the nine cards under the home page's features heading were its siblings, not its
  children).
%>
<% item_heading = section['heading'].present? ? 'h3' : 'h2' %>
<% source = section['source'].to_s %>
<% if Marketing::SectionSchema::SOURCES.include?(source) %>
  <% scope = source.to_sym %>
  <% entries = Marketing::Catalog.entries(scope) %>
  <% limit = section['limit'].to_i %>
  <% entries = entries.first(limit) if limit.positive? %>
  <% index_href = marketing_target_href("page:standing:#{source}") %>

  <%# THE CHANNELS' OWN MARKS, from Marketing::ChannelBrand.
      This used to be a hash of ten `i-lucide-*` names under a rule that said the channel is named in text
      beside the mark, so a neutral glyph is clearer and needs no trademark. The result was nine recognisable
      logos rendered as nine grey outlines -- three of them the SAME outline, because Lucide has no Messenger
      and no LINE -- and it is the single largest reason the site reads as less alive than the page it
      replaced. A brand mark used to name the brand it belongs to is nominative use; it is also simply what a
      reader is looking for when they scan a list of channels for the one they use.

      MARKED CHANNELS ONLY. `marked?` is false for a scope that is not channels and for an id with no mark,
      and an entry without one renders with no tile rather than with a stand-in: a meaningless glyph repeated
      down a column is worse than a column of text. %>

  <section class="<%= tone %>">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <%= render 'marketing/shared/section_head', heading: section['heading'], lede: section['lede'] %>

      <% case section['style'].to_s %>
      <% when 'chips' %>
        <ul class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
          <% entries.each do |entry| %>
            <li class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-lyn-line bg-lyn-paper py-1.5 pe-4 ps-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-lyn-ink">
              <% if scope == :channels && Marketing::ChannelBrand.marked?(entry.id) %>
                <%= render 'marketing/shared/channel_mark', id: entry.id, size: 28, labelled: false %>
              <% end %>
              <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.name") %>
              <%= render 'marketing/shared/state_badge', state: entry.state %>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>

      <% when 'list' %>
        <ul class="mt-12 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <% entries.each do |entry| %>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <% if scope == :channels && Marketing::ChannelBrand.marked?(entry.id) %>
                <div class="mt-0.5 shrink-0">
                  <%= render 'marketing/shared/channel_mark', id: entry.id, size: 44, labelled: false %>
                </div>
              <% end %>
              <div class="min-w-0">
                <%= content_tag item_heading, class: 'flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-lg font-semibold text-lyn-ink' do %>
                  <% if entry.detail? %>
                    <a class="transition-colors hover:text-lyn-royal focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue"
                       href="<%= marketing_entry_path(scope, entry) %>">
                      <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.name") %>
                    </a>
                  <% else %>
                    <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.name") %>
                  <% end %>
                  <%= render 'marketing/shared/state_badge', state: entry.state %>
                <% end %>
                <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-[1.75] text-lyn-ink-soft">
                  <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.summary") %>
                </p>
                <% if t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.requires", default: nil).present? %>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-lyn-ink-soft/80">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-lyn-ink-soft">
                      <%= t(scope == :channels ? 'marketing.state.you_supply' : 'marketing.state.requires') %>
                    </span>
                    <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.requires") %>
                  </p>
                <% end %>
              </div>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>

      <% else %>
        <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <% entries.each do |entry| %>
            <%= render 'marketing/shared/entry_card', entry: entry, scope: scope, heading_level: item_heading %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <% if section['link_label'].present? && index_href.present? %>
        <a href="<%= index_href %>"
           class="mt-10 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-royal transition-colors hover:text-lyn-ink focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue">
          <%= section['link_label'] %>
        </a>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>
<% end %>
